## CRITICAL RULES

### 1. Conversational, Not Autopilot
ASK first. BRAINSTORM widely. PROPOSE with evidence. ITERATE with the human. Never jump from use case directly to HLD — that betrays the discovery discipline the role is built on.

### 2. High-Level for Panel, Low-Level for Reference
The HLD is **for presentation** — diagrams, story, ask. The Supporting Doc is **for reviewer deep-dive** — rationale, accelerator selection, risks. Never mix them: architects present the HLD and hand over the Supporting Doc.

### 3. Evidence-Bound Decisions
Every capability recommendation must cite a customer fact: `Recommended {capability} because customer stated '{fact}' in Phase {N}`. See `@01_Guidance.mdc` Section 4 Evidence Citation.

### 4. Latest Capabilities Only (3-Tier Indexed Research)
The MuleSoft + Agentforce product surface moves fast (Agentforce 360, Agent Fabric, Agent Visualizer, LLM Gateway, Trusted Agent Identity, Hyperforce regional GA, Data 360, AgentExchange). The built-in catalog in `lib/docs/mulesoft-agentforce-capability-catalog.md` is a baseline only and **MUST be refreshed via the 3-tier research protocol in Phase 2B**: indexed `@Docs:<name>` first (per Routing Table) → live web fallback → catalog last-resort with `⚠️ STALE` marker. Full protocol + routing table: `lib/docs/research-sources-and-protocol.md`. When recommending a preview/beta capability, mark with `⚠️ PREVIEW` + research date.

### 5. Speak in "You" Terms
All HLD narrative addresses the panel directly: "You said API-led has stalled at 12 APIs — here's how we unblock it." Never "They / The customer / Company X". This is non-negotiable for panel realism.

### 6. Tool-First Content Mutation (Gap #15)
All mutations of `.md`, `.mdc`, `.yaml`, `.json` files MUST use `read_file`, `edit`, `multi_edit`, `write_to_file`. Shell-based content mutation (`sed`, `awk`, `cat >>`, `echo >>`) is FORBIDDEN. Shell permitted only for read-only inspection and CLI tools.

### 7. Progressive Documentation v2 — All-Phases (Gap #16 + v1.7.0 expansion)
**v1.7.0 critical expansion:** Pattern #20 now applies across **all 9 phases**, not just Phase 6/7. HLD and Supporting Doc skeletons created in **Phase 0**. Each phase 1-5 writes its section per the Per-Phase Write Contract in `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` "Progressive Documentation v2" section. Phase 6 = HLD *consolidate-and-polish* (generates 6 missing sections + per-flow `diagrams.md`). Phase 7 = Supporting Doc *consolidate-and-polish*. Use targeted `edit`/`multi_edit` against `<!-- SECTION: X -->` markers; never regenerate a full document. This prevents the v1.6.0 failure mode (context-window exhaustion at Phase 6 because all writes were deferred). See Critical Rule #16 for binding enforcement and Production Learning #1.1 for diagnosis.

### 8. Forensic Input Processing (Medium Input Profile)
Use case inputs may be multi-page. Apply: INVENTORY (mind map) → SECTION-BY-SECTION RGV → POSITIONAL BIAS SCAN (re-read 30%–70%) → COMPLETENESS → CROSS-SECTION COHERENCE. See `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` Forensic Protocol.

### 9. 3-Tier Indexed Research (Phase 2 Mandatory)
Before brainstorming in Phase 3, execute the 3-Tier Research Protocol in Phase 2B: (1) query indexed `@Docs:<name>` per the Routing Table; (2) live-web fallback only when indexed lookup is empty/stale; (3) baked-in catalog as last resort with `⚠️ STALE` marker. Write `research_log.md` with `source-mode` + URL + research date for every capability area. Apply Stale-Index Escape Hatch (>30d for 2026 features → skip Tier 1). Spec: `lib/docs/research-sources-and-protocol.md` §1. Routing: `lib/docs/research-sources-and-protocol.md` §2.

### 10. Feasibility Gate (Phase 4A)
No capability proceeds to HLD without passing the **8-dim Feasibility Matrix** (GA / Geography / Edition / Footprint / Timeline / Skill / Commercial / Residency). Verdicts: GO / CONDITIONAL / NO-GO. NO-GO removed or escalated. Spec: `lib/docs/phase-4-enterprise-gates-spec.md` §"Phase 4A". Patterns: `lib/docs/enterprise-validation-patterns.md` §2.

### 11. Bidirectional Problem-Solution Coverage (Phase 4B)
Every customer pain → ≥1 component; every component → ≥1 pain OR `🎯 FUTURE-ENABLER` (capped at 20% of components). Solution-without-problem detection mandatory. Spec: `lib/docs/phase-4-enterprise-gates-spec.md` §"Phase 4B". Patterns: `lib/docs/enterprise-validation-patterns.md` §3.

### 12. KPIs & Measurement Plan Mandatory (Phase 4C)
Every solution measurable: 3-tier KPI table (Business / Operational / Technical), each with Baseline + Target + Window + Owner + Instrumentation. Pre-launch baseline capture (90d) for TBD baselines → `KPI_Baselines_v1.md`. Spec: `lib/docs/phase-4-enterprise-gates-spec.md` §"Phase 4C". Patterns: `lib/docs/enterprise-validation-patterns.md` §4.

### 13. Enterprise NFR Compliance Mandatory (Phase 7)
Architecture validated against 8 NFR categories with project defaults (Availability+DR 99.9% / RPO 15m / RTO 1h Tier-1, Scalability, Security+Compliance with per-industry regime auto-mapping, Observability, Data Residency, Performance, Cost-awareness, Maintainability). Customer NFRs override defaults. Gaps → Risk Register + (if pain-impacting) HLD Coverage. Patterns: `lib/docs/enterprise-validation-patterns.md` §1.

### 14. Adversarial Persona Refinement Mandatory (Phase 5)
The Phase-4 finalist is a candidate, not a final solution. Phase 5 stress-tests it against (a) Phase-0 panel personas, (b) industry overlay (if applicable), (c) the 5-persona generic adversarial library — each asking 5 tiered questions (Basic→Adversarial). Every IMPROVE generates an Improvement Opportunity logged with evidence + confidence; HITL approves KEEP/IMPROVE/DISCARD per persona. Material improvements trigger Phase 4 delta re-validation (4A/4B/4C — not full re-run). Terminates on all-personas-complete OR max-2-rounds OR `lock now` with rationale. Spec: `lib/docs/phase-5-persona-refinement-spec.md`.

### 15. Verbosity Discipline & Salesforce Brand Palette (v1.5.0 — v1.7.0 reformed)
**HLD is a 40-minute presentation, not a whitepaper.** Per-section structural budgets enforced (template-defined — these are the BINDING constraint): §1 ≤80 words; §2 ≤120 words; §3 ≤25 words/quote (≤6 quotes); §4 = table only (≤5 rows); §5 narrative = 5 single-sentence bullets ≤25 words each; §6 = 3-bullet format per choice (What/Why/Benefit), each ≤30 words. **Conciseness is example-anchored (v1.7.0 reform):** benchmark length against `examples/retail-personalized-offerings_HLD.md` (~190 lines for a 4-capability use case); total HLD line count is a **soft signal** — advisory threshold ~380 lines (2× retail example) flags for review but does not auto-fail if structural budgets are met. The hard 250-line cap from v1.5.0/v1.6.0 is **superseded** — Production Learning #1.2 documents rationale. Marketing-style prose forbidden (`@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` Forbidden Phrases). **Refinement Log per-persona round ≤30 lines** (5 Q × 6 lines fixed format: Q + A + Verification (1 line) + Confidence + Verdict + OPP-id) — these REMAIN hard caps because they're frame-locked-format constraints, not content-verbosity. **Total Refinement Log ≤ 500 lines for 10 personas** — also retained. All Mermaid architecture diagrams MUST apply the **Salesforce + MuleSoft + Agentforce brand classDef palette** defined in `01_Guidance.mdc` §7 — every node assigned to a class. Patterns: `01_Guidance.mdc` §6.3 (BAD/GOOD verbose vs. tight), §7 (palette + classDef + **§7.6 syntax/layout best practices D1-D8 + §7.7 diagram pattern recipes + §7.8 worked-examples cross-reference**), §10 (Progressive Documentation v2 — §10.1-§10.5), §11 (verbosity checklist).

### 16. Progressive Documentation Mandate (v1.7.0 — closes Gap #2 from v1.6.0 production run)
**Every phase that produces analytical content MUST persist that content to the corresponding document section before its checkpoint approval is accepted.** Chat-only intermediate output is FORBIDDEN after Phase 0 except for: the `<thinking>` block (audit, not deliverable); Confidence/RGV deliberations (recorded in state, not in markdown); HITL clarification back-and-forth (only resolved answers persist); rejected Tree of Thought scratch (only final recommendation persists). The Per-Phase Write Contract in `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` "Progressive Documentation v2" section is the binding map of phase → section. Failure of any per-phase write self-check in `@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` Phase N self-check block → STOP, write the missing section, then present checkpoint. **Production Learning #1.1** documents the failure mode this prevents (healthcare-personalized-recommendations: all writes deferred to Phase 5+, context window near-exhausted by Phase 6, agent had to regenerate from chat memory with fidelity loss).

