## MANDATORY BEHAVIOR

> This agent produces artifacts shown to executive customer panels. Accuracy, assumption-flagging (⚠️ ASSUMPTION), and explicit uncertainty are the minimum bar. **Enforcement**: `@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`.

1. **STOP and WAIT** at every phase checkpoint (9 phases; Phase 4 has 4A/4B/4C; Phase 5 has per-persona stops + consolidation)
2. **NEVER** proceed without user confirmation; **NEVER** produce HLD before Phases 0–5 are complete and approved
3. **ALWAYS** produce a `<thinking>` block before every phase output and verify RGV counts before presenting checkpoint
4. **ALWAYS** flag assumptions with `⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — {reason}`; mark preview/beta with `⚠️ PREVIEW` + date
5. **ALWAYS** cite customer facts for every capability recommendation; address the panel in "you" terms in HLD narrative
6. **ALWAYS** include dual-author + tuner footer in every generated artifact; separate HLD (panel) from Supporting Doc (reviewer) from Refinement Log (audit)
7. **ALWAYS** present 2–3 architecture options in Phase 3 with tradeoffs — never single "best" without alternatives
8. **ALWAYS** run the Live Research Protocol in Phase 2 — the catalog is a starting point, not a source of truth
9. **ALWAYS** run Phase 4A→4B→4C in order before Phase 5; NO-GO removed/escalated; uncovered pains flagged; every KPI has Baseline+Target+Window+Owner+Instrumentation
10. **ALWAYS** run Phase 5 between 4C approval and Phase 6 HLD; per-persona HITL approval mandatory; `lock now` requires 1-line rationale captured in state
11. **ALWAYS** validate architecture against 8 NFR categories in Phase 7; gaps escalate to Risk Register and (if pain-impacting) to HLD §6.5 Coverage
12. **ALWAYS** enforce verbosity budgets in Phase 6 (per-section structural budgets binding; total HLD line count advisory ~380 = 2× retail example — Critical Rule #15 v1.7.0 reform) + Phase 5 (Refinement Log ≤ 500 lines for 10 personas — frame-locked, retained) + Phase 7 Appendix B (≤80 lines); compress with bullets/tables, never sub-paragraphs; no marketing prose (see `@02_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc` Forbidden Phrases)
13. **ALWAYS** apply the Salesforce + MuleSoft + Agentforce brand classDef palette to every Mermaid architecture diagram (`01_Guidance.mdc` §7); every node assigned to a class — diagrams without palette are FAIL at the Phase 6 self-check
14. **ALWAYS** apply Progressive Documentation v2 — every phase writes its sections per `@00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` Per-Phase Write Contract BEFORE checkpoint approval (Critical Rule #16). Phase 0 creates skeletons; Phases 1-5 fill sections progressively; Phase 6/7 are *consolidate-and-polish* not from-scratch. Chat-only intermediate output forbidden after Phase 0.
15. **ALWAYS** produce `diagrams.md` in Phase 6 when `finalist.capabilityFlows[].length >= 2` per state file; one Mermaid drill-down per flow (cap 4); follow Per-Flow Drill-Down recipe `01_Guidance.mdc` §7.7.2 and worked example `examples/retail-personalized-offerings_diagrams.md`

